[Music]  making shop is about redesigning the way  we produce  the way we retail to allow the last  small production  to be in the shop environment so we  won't have to produce  until there is a demand for it  community design is actually ironically  something not very new  back in the 70s and 80s actually we  called it kampung spirit which is  largely basically communities themselves  were  responding to whatever issues they had  maybe the way that singapore developed  became more structural  communities no longer learned how to  respond by themselves they'll be working  with healthcare institutions to see  whether or not  communities have their own responses to  their own healthcare challenges  the local tree project was started to  reduce waste and bring value to the  community  we want to eradicate the throwaway  culture that we have and produce  furniture  and objects that people feel proud to  have  our project is about reducing single use  plastic weights from food packaging  mainly deliveries and takeaways  and we focus on hawker centers where a  majority of our population eats  [Music]  the ongoing r d at the moment is focused  on finding out  how we can strengthen and stabilize this  timber by using sustainable energy  mediums  as this research is heavy on data and  scientific tests  we gained many beneficial numbers along  the way  the project we think was really quite  challenging because we need to speak to  different citizens we may not have  personal relationships with  we've had 119 interviews so far i would  say out of those 190 we've got maybe 30  to 40 really solid interviews where  people are willing to speak  we conducted behavioral research to  understand  how we can make these containers better  for the eating experience  and we also had a number of in-depth  interview with the consumers as well as  hawkers  [Music]  the good design research sponsorship  from design singapore council  was really phenomenal in helping us  begin to just get a kickstart  it has allowed us also to move on to  building up a strong prototype really to  actually pass over to  to real stakeholders as an established  brand  we struggle to find time to work on our  innovation  good design research initiative allows  us to take time off  and to work towards our innovation  our ideas and we must keep innovating in  order to move forward  the good design research initiative has  strengthened our position  this helps improve and differentiate us  allowing us to add value to our products  and customers  [Music]  we hope to achieve a very polished  experience to our customers where they  can come  and see their products being done in a  magical way  we hope to partner with nea to implement  in hawker centers we want to  see these ideas being rolled out and  making positive change  the hope is really to bring it to other  precincts within the country to look at  other kinds of problems  it may not be health it could be mental  health it could be basically youth  delinquency  we're planning to continue working on  research and development for our local  trees  finding other methods to salvage parts  of the trees  or buying products they are normally  thrown away hopefully  we can create a positive domino effect  that drives our sunset industry towards  a more circular future  [Music]

